meta {
  name: 04 Payer B credential on payer A route - EXPECT 403
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{gateway}}/payera/outbound/Patient?_count=5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  _count: 5
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{tokB_forA}}
  Accept: application/fhir+json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 403
}

docs {
  Assertion 4. The headline result.

  The token in this request is the one Entra issued in request 02 - valid
  signature, correct audience, not expired, not forged.

  Layer 2 reads the appid claim, looks it up in the entitlement named value,
  finds "payerb", compares it to the payer implied by the route, and refuses.

  This is the difference between a boundary that trusts the token and a
  boundary that checks entitlement. Entra answered "who are you". Only the
  gateway answers "and are you allowed to be here".
}
